{
  "schema": "headroom.circuit.v1",
  "id": "ehx-small-stone",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Electro-Harmonix Small Stone (Issue J, CA3094)",
  "description": "Electro-Harmonix Small Stone, Issue J (1977) circuit: five CA3094 (house-marked EH1048) OTA + Darlington chips on a 9 V battery. Vbias 3.6 V from R3 15 kΩ / R1 10 kΩ with C1 33 µF. Input: R4 100 kΩ, C2 6.8 nF into a 2N5088 / 2N5087 feedback pair (Q1 CE with R6 10 kΩ, Q2 PNP collector driving R42 4.7 kΩ back to Q1's emitter over R7 4.7 kΩ: gain 2), C3 10 µF into four OTA all-pass stages. Each stage: input resistor (30 kΩ first, 27 kΩ others) and output feedback 27 kΩ into the OTA inverting input (pin 2), 1 kΩ from there to Vbias, pin 3 at Vbias, a 6.8 nF cap from the stage input to the OTA output (pin 1), and the on-chip Darlington (Q12/Q13, internal R1 2 kΩ and R2 47 kΩ) as the output follower into 10 kΩ. Mixer: dry R8 30 kΩ from the preamp and wet R13 27 kΩ from stage 4, C7 0.1 µF / R14 470 kΩ to the output (no output buffer). Color switch pole B: on = R11 3.3 kΩ / R12 4.7 kΩ / R10 27 kΩ / C6 0.1 µF feedback from stage 4 into the R4/C2 junction; off = that network grounded and R9 270 kΩ loads the input node. LFO: IC5 CA3094 integrating its output current (IABC set through the 1 MΩ Rate rheostat from the R22 27 kΩ / R23 7.5 kΩ divider) on C12 33 µF; its Darlington emitter drives the four stage IABC pins (pin 5) through R24 100 Ω, and the Darlington collector current (the total stage IABC) returns into the Q3/Q4 2N5087 cross-coupled trigger (R15 4.7 kΩ, R17 15 kΩ, R18 1 kΩ, R19 27 kΩ, R20 1.8 kΩ, C10 0.1 µF) that sets IC5's input polarity. Color pole A switches R16 22 kΩ (off) or the C10 node (on) onto the trigger. The bypass footswitch is the host's unit bypass.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "R. G. Keen, 'EH Small Stone Phaser Issue J' schematic (as compiled in 'All Electro-Harmonix Effects', Experimentalists Anonymous): all Issue J values, CA3094 pin use, Color switch wiring, 9 V battery, R23 7.5k, 'house marked EH1048 ... can be replaced with CA3094'",
      "url": "https://experimentalistsanonymous.com/diy/Schematics/Miscellaneous/All%20Electro-Harmonix%20Effects.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "General Guitar Gadgets, 'Electro-Harmonix Small Stone' (Issue J, R. G. Keen drawing with JD Sleep reference designators, 2007): designators used here; it reads R23 as 2.5k",
      "url": "http://www.generalguitargadgets.com/pdf/ggg_smallstj_sc.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "Aion FX, 'Sunstone OTA Phaser' build documentation v1.1.0 (Issue J adaptation): CA3094 Darlington drawn discretely (2 kΩ collector resistor, 47 kΩ emitter resistor), trigger and rate network values, Rate pot 1MC (reverse log), 2002 reissue Color changes",
      "url": "https://aionfx.com/app/files/docs/sunstone_documentation.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "Intersil CA3094/A/B datasheet FN598: pinout (1 OTA output / compensation, 2 inverting, 3 non-inverting for the pin-6 'source' output, 4 V−, 5 IABC, 6 Darlington emitter, 7 V+, 8 Darlington collector), internal R1 2 kΩ and R2 47 kΩ, VABC 0.68 V at 100 µA, gm 2.2 mS at IABC 100 µA, composite hFE 16 000 min / 100 000 typ",
      "url": "https://www.experimentalistsanonymous.com/diy/Datasheets/CA3094.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "A. Carson, C. Valentini-Botinhao, S. King, S. Bilbao, 'Differentiable grey-box modelling of phaser effects using frame-based spectral processing', DAFx-23 paper 38: Small Stone topology (LFO, four first-order all-pass sections, Color feedback loop) and measured LFO rates (Table 1)",
      "url": "https://www.dafx.de/paper-archive/2023/DAFx23_paper_38.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "A. Huovilainen, 'Enhanced digital models for analog modulation effects', DAFx-05: OTA all-pass stage law of the Small Stone",
      "url": "https://www.dafx.de/paper-archive/2005/P_155.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "Freestompboxes, 'Electro Harmonix Small Stone V1': EH1048 OTAs, version history (V1 1974-78 with two LFO OTAs; Issue J)",
      "url": "https://www.freestompboxes.org/viewtopic.php?t=24786"
    },
    {
      "title": "Fairchild 2N5087 SPICE card (IS 6.734f BF 254.1 BR 2.683 VAF 45.7 ISE 6.734f NE 1.741 CJE 7.5p CJC 6.2p), as distributed in the LTspice standard.bjt library (licence not stated; quoted as a factual parameter set)",
      "url": "https://github.com/polimi-ispl/mxrphase90/blob/main/LTspice/standard.bjt"
    }
  ],
  "io": {
    "input": "in",
    "output": "out",
    "inputVoltsPerFS": 1.0,
    "outputVoltsPerFS": 1.0
  },
  "oversampling": 1,
  "solver": "dk",
  "models": {
    "2N5087": {
      "kind": "pnp",
      "is": 6.734e-15,
      "bf": 254.1,
      "br": 2.683,
      "vaf": 45.7,
      "ise": 6.734e-15,
      "ne": 1.741,
      "cje": 7.5e-12,
      "cjc": 6.2e-12,
      "note": "Fairchild 2N5087 SPICE card (LTspice standard.bjt); IKF, RB/RC, TF/TR and junction grading omitted"
    },
    "CA3094_Q_TYP": {
      "kind": "npn",
      "is": 1e-14,
      "bf": 316,
      "br": 1,
      "note": "unverified: CA3094 output Darlington die (Q12, Q13). D: the datasheet gives only the composite hFE (16 000 min, 100 000 typ at 50 mA), so each die gets sqrt(100 000) = 316. IS is a generic small-signal value. Overrides the library CA3094_Q (hFE 100), whose 1e4 composite gain would pull ~40 nA of base current out of the stage integrator nodes and ~0.1 µA out of the 33 µF LFO cap",
      "cje": 2e-12,
      "cjc": 1e-12
    }
  },
  "controls": [
    {
      "id": "rate",
      "label": "Rate",
      "kind": "continuous",
      "default": 0.5,
      "params": [
        "Rt"
      ],
      "group": "Main",
      "note": "R21 1 MΩ Rate pot wired as a rheostat from the R22 27 kΩ / R23 7.5 kΩ divider (Thevenin 1.96 V, 5.9 kΩ) into IC5's IABC pin; clockwise = less resistance = more IABC = faster. Reverse-log (C) taper per the Aion Issue J adaptation. DAFx-23 measured 0.086 / 0.625 / 2.28 Hz at 9 / 12 / 3 o'clock (Color off)"
    },
    {
      "id": "color",
      "label": "Color",
      "kind": "switch",
      "default": 0,
      "params": [
        "Cl"
      ],
      "group": "Main",
      "note": "DPDT Color switch. On (1): pole B closes the R11/R12/R10/C6 feedback loop from stage 4 into the R4/C2 junction (resonant, deeper sweep); pole A ties the trigger's R18 node to the C10 node (DAFx-23: slower and deeper LFO with Color on). Off (0): pole B grounds the feedback network's C6 end so R9 270 kΩ loads the input node; pole A puts R16 22 kΩ across R17 15 kΩ. Legacy float: >= 0.5 is on"
    },
    {
      "id": "sync",
      "label": "Sync",
      "kind": "continuous",
      "default": 0.0,
      "params": [
        "Sy"
      ],
      "legacyOnly": true,
